## SEC — capability flow

### S1 — No shim re-grant — PASS
`llvm_link_shim.oo` has no `oo_cap_grant_sys`. `_shim.ll` wrappers pass
caller `%cap` into `oo_path_exists` / `oo_read_file` / `oo_sys_exec`.
Preamble still *declares* `@oo_cap_grant_sys` for `main` only
(`llvm_emit_preamble.oo` line 74; `llvm_emit_fn.oo` lines 183–185). That
is not a shim re-grant on `sys_exec` / `read_file` / `path_exists`.

### S2 — `&FsCap` / `&SysCap` remain on check_cache / check_mod — PASS
Cited in C1. `check_cache_hit` / `check_cache_read` keep `fs: &FsCap`
(`check_cache.oo` lines 32, 39). Call sites still `path_exists(fs, …)`,
`read_file(fs, …)`, `sys_exec(sys, …)` (`check_cache.oo` lines 23, 37, 47,
61). No cap parameter was deleted.

## Residual (must not be hidden)

  - Other `oodac/llvm_emit*.oo` files stay dirty from the prior LLVM-link
    slice. They are not this stamp-walk write set.
  - Stamp-walk of a valid `g_` listing is the claim. LLVM typecheck of
    hello after a stale listing may print `ERR	check	empty`.
  - C emit + gcc remains the product path. Full gcc-parity is residual.
  - Do not tick OPEN-68 closed on this note.

## Verdict
PASS. Do not claim OPEN-68 closed. Do not claim C emit gone. Do not claim
gcc retired. C1–C7 and SEC cap-flow PASS on cited sources, IR, COORD
git/stat, and the 2090456-byte side ELF.
